# A lens whose focus is a library's type: `put` writes a Decimal into the file and `get` gives it back inside an Entry.
# The route of the exported struct is its public functions, each called by its caller, run on the Ledger `new` built.
# What `get` reads and parses are steps of their own, a library's operations whose results the body names; the amount
# is of no type the code writes, so it is `_`.

route books.Ledger
step Ledger()/Ledger.new
known #74 step Ledger()/Ledger.new/Ledger()                      # the struct built by its literal
step Ledger()/Ledger.put
step Ledger()/Ledger.get
step Ledger()/Ledger.get/read_to_string
step Ledger()/Ledger.get/map_err                                 # `Decimal::from_str(text.trim()).map_err(..)`, named `amount`
step Ledger()/Ledger.get/Entry()

line entry > Ledger()/Ledger.new call
line entry > Ledger()/Ledger.put call
line entry > Ledger()/Ledger.get call

line Ledger()/Ledger.new/Ledger() > Ledger@Ledger()/Ledger.new/Ledger() value
line Ledger@Ledger()/Ledger.new/Ledger() > Ledger()/Ledger.new value
line Ledger()/Ledger.new > Ledger@Ledger()/Ledger.new value
line Ledger@Ledger()/Ledger.new > Ledger()/Ledger.put value
line Ledger@Ledger()/Ledger.new > Ledger()/Ledger.get value

known #new line Decimal·amount > Ledger()/Ledger.put value       # new-A: put's parameter, a library's type
line Ledger()/Ledger.put > Disk(self.path) own

line Disk(self.path) > Ledger()/Ledger.get own
line Ledger()/Ledger.get/read_to_string > _·text@Ledger()/Ledger.get/read_to_string value
known #new line _·text@Ledger()/Ledger.get/read_to_string > Ledger()/Ledger.get/map_err value   # new-C: from_str's result goes into map_err
line Ledger()/Ledger.get/map_err > _·amount@Ledger()/Ledger.get/map_err value
line _·amount@Ledger()/Ledger.get/map_err > Ledger()/Ledger.get/Entry() value
line Ledger()/Ledger.get/Entry() > Entry@Ledger()/Ledger.get/Entry() value
line Entry@Ledger()/Ledger.get/Entry() > Ledger()/Ledger.get value
line Ledger()/Ledger.get > Entry@Ledger()/Ledger.get value

home Ledger@Ledger()/Ledger.new/Ledger() Ledger()/Ledger.new
home Ledger@Ledger()/Ledger.new Ledger()
known #new home Decimal·amount Ledger()
home _·text@Ledger()/Ledger.get/read_to_string Ledger()/Ledger.get
home _·amount@Ledger()/Ledger.get/map_err Ledger()/Ledger.get
home Entry@Ledger()/Ledger.get/Entry() Ledger()/Ledger.get
home Entry@Ledger()/Ledger.get Ledger()

side entry left
side Disk(self.path) between

# building the exported struct runs its public functions, `new` among them, so the literal is read as recursive
known #74 extra step Ledger()/Ledger.new/Ledger() recursive
# new-A: the parameter of a function the entry calls has lost its name
known #new extra line Decimal > Ledger()/Ledger.put value
known #new extra home Decimal Ledger()
# new-C: a call whose result goes into the named call around it is a step of its own
known #new extra step Ledger()/Ledger.get/from_str
known #new extra line _·text@Ledger()/Ledger.get/read_to_string > Ledger()/Ledger.get/from_str value
known #new extra line Ledger()/Ledger.get/from_str > _·amount@Ledger()/Ledger.get/from_str value
known #new extra line _·amount@Ledger()/Ledger.get/from_str > Ledger()/Ledger.get/map_err value
known #new extra home _·amount@Ledger()/Ledger.get/from_str Ledger()/Ledger.get
